  {
    "@id": "https://www.ensemblecaprice.com/concert/cinqueme-de-beethoven",
    "http://ogp.me/ns#description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Beethoven's Fifth Symphony, with its unforgettable opening notes, embodies both trial and triumph, while Mozart's Great Mass in C minor unfolds with unparalleled dramatic power.\nDive into the heart of the musical genius of two of the greatest classical composers, performed by Ensemble Caprice and four exceptional soloists. To complete the program, Mozart’s enchanting Ave verum will be sung by the outstanding Ensemble ArtChoral. Under the inspired direction of Matthias Maute, this evening promises to blend brilliance and intensity, offering a striking and unforgettable musical experience. A unique opportunity to experience the splendor of classical music in all its magnificence!\n\nProgram:Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart, Great Mass in C Minor, K. 427Ludwig van Beethoven, Symphony No. 5 in C minor, Op. 67Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart, Ave verum corpus, K. 618"
      }
