  {
    "@id": "https://www.ensemblecaprice.com/concert/b9-mtl",
    "http://ogp.me/ns#description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "This Valentine's Day, let yourself be seduced by the grandeur and passion of Beethoven's immortal choral masterpiece, Symphony No. 9, in a spectacular performance by Ensemble Caprice and Ensemble ArtChoral. A true testament to the triumph of the human spirit over adversity, with its emblematic final movement \"Ode to Joy\", discover the emotions of Beethoven's visionary composition, under the direction of conductor Matthias Maute. The program also includes Fanny Mendelssohn's cantata Hiob and a premiere by William Kraushaar.  An evening of musical passion and chocolates a plenty!\n\nProgram:\nLudwig van Beethoven, Symphony No. 9 in D minor, op. 125\nFanny Mendelssohn-Hensel, Hiob (Cantata)\nWilliam Kraushaar, World Premiere - Ensemble Caprice Commission"
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#image": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://static.wixstatic.com/media/143a34_7193e44721304149b1076424aa9ef7b1~mv2.png/v1/fit/w_2500,h_1330,al_c/143a34_7193e44721304149b1076424aa9ef7b1~mv2.png"
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#image:width": [
